<!DOCTYPE airframe SYSTEM "../airframe.dtd">
<airframe name="Skyhawk">
  <description>
    Scale model fixedwing airframe EDF equipped with a mRo Pixracer flightcontroller hardware

    + Model:       Alfa Model A4 Skyhawk
    + Autopilot:   PX4FMU 4.0 in the form of a mRo Pixracer v1.0 R15
    + Actuators:   Basic 4g servos
    + GNSS         Ublox M10N GNSS
    + MAG          None
    + ESC:         ARIA 70 AM32 Brushless ESC
    + RCRX:        OpenRXSR Receiver
    + AIRSPEED:    Sensirion SDP33
    + TELEMETRY:   Hope SiK module
    + CURRENT:     3DR clone powerbrick
    + RANGEFINDER: Sonar GY-US42v2
    + MOTOR:       4300 RPM/V Outrunner Brushless on 12blade EDF
    + PROP:        12 Blade EDF
    + BATTERY:     18650 Samsung Li-Ion 3S1P 3500mAh 30A

    NOTES:
    + Using Enhanced Total Energy control as control loop in Final AC
    + Servo pins point to back of airframe
    + Engine battery voltage and current values via separate sensor
    + Flightcontroller powered via Powerbrick BEC
    + Telemetry powered via FC
    + Si10xx Chip based with firmware enabling PPRZ RSSI message
    + Uploading of the firmware can be performed via original PX4 bootloader...
      Simple, USB cable in, upload... voila PPRZ aircraft on a Pixracer...

    + GNSS set to ~17Hz update rate, 4 constelations, SBAS enabled
    + Advised battery for this airframe is a 3500mAh 3S LiPo min. 15C
    + If testing "Classic" (as in not ETECS..) make sure to disable the settings/estimation/ac_char
    + Set the USE_AIRSPEED value to FALSE at first, for no airspeed tests
    + Use also flightplan_versatile if no airspeed sensor is ues and use flightplan versatile_unified only with enabled airspeed sensor
  </description>

